attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a long spine.** Columns 0 to 49, `rhoL` to `phoU`, are carried by 92 to 100% of chromosomes, all persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0 to 25% of calls {S1}. The model names 54 to 100% of them, fewest at column 47, `pstA`, 54% {S1}.

@variable **The middle is a fork and variable stretch**, columns 50 to 57, all shell, carried by 47 to 72%, the most plastic stretch of the window {S2, P}. Through columns 55 to 57 a branch of 3 families runs in 10 to 19%, [[type III effector]] {S2.b55, Q}. The spine between, columns 58 to 73, `yieH` to `dnaN`, is [[phosphate transport]] at columns 45 to 48 {S3, S1, Q}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 96 against 88%, and hesitates less there, 0.17 against 0.44 bits {M}. Its most hesitant column, 5, `ppiC`, is a spine column, at 0.79 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends on fork and variable columns.** Columns 74 to 79, `recF` to `dgoR`, are carried by 20 to 90%, 4 persistent, 2 shell {S4}. The last column is `dgoR`, in 43% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 95% of genes**, 0.22 bits on average, perplexity 1.3 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 0.79 against 0.15 bits, and names fewer genes, 80% against 96% {C}.

